> It may be sleep deprivation kicking in hehe, but can't really spot what "not dependencies" does.

Just FYI:

There is a special test in some test files (e.g. quantum and chemistry backends) that checks if all dependencies are installed (and therefore that no test is skipped)
```python
@pytest.mark.dependencies
def test_dependencies():
    for package in tequila.simulators.simulator_api.SUPPORTED_BACKENDS:
        if package not in ["qulacs_gpu", "qiskit_gpu"]:
            assert (package in tq.simulators.simulator_api.INSTALLED_BACKENDS)
```

with the "no dependencies" flag that test is skipped (so in principle it should not be set for ci_backends, think I deactivated it once due some issues with pyquil and the virtual machine). 

You can ignore that.
